the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the person id of the parameters is *a text*.
    the benefit of the parameters is *a text*.
    the check result is *a truth value*.
    the person enrolled in benefit service result is *a truth value*.

the templates are:
    the enrollments of the situation include *a person id* with *a benefit*.
    the enrollments of the situation are listed.

the knowledge base person_not_enrolled_in_benefit includes:

the text of the_model is at "sources/person-not-enrolled-in-benefit.dmn".

rule person_enrolled_in_benefit_service_1 with provenance the model at decision PersonEnrolledInBenefitService:
the person enrolled in benefit service result is true if
    the enrollments of the situation are listed
    and the enrollments of the situation include a person id with a benefit
    and the person id is equal to the person id of the parameters
    and the benefit is equal to the benefit of the parameters.

rule person_enrolled_in_benefit_service_2 with provenance the model at decision PersonEnrolledInBenefitService:
the person enrolled in benefit service result is false if
    the enrollments of the situation are listed
    and the person id of the parameters is a text
    and the benefit of the parameters is a second text
    and it is not the case that
        the enrollments of the situation include a person id with a benefit
        and the person id of the parameters is a third text
        and the person id is equal to the third text
        and the benefit of the parameters is a fourth text
        and the benefit is equal to the fourth text.

rule check_result_1 with provenance the model at decision checkResult:
the check result is true if
    the person enrolled in benefit service result is false.

rule check_result_2 with provenance the model at decision checkResult:
the check result is false if
    the person enrolled in benefit service result is true.

scenario Enrolled is, as stated in the Bruno requests of PersonNotEnrolledInBenefit at test case Enrolled:
    the benefit of the parameters is "bogus".
    the person id of the parameters is "p1".
    the enrollments of the situation are listed.
    the enrollments of the situation include "p1" with "bogus".
    q_d_check_result expects answers ["the check result is false"].

scenario Enrollments_empty is, as stated in the Bruno requests of PersonNotEnrolledInBenefit at test case Enrollments empty:
    the benefit of the parameters is "bogus".
    the person id of the parameters is "p1".
    the enrollments of the situation are listed.
    q_d_check_result expects answers ["the check result is true"].

scenario Enrollments_null is, as stated in the Bruno requests of PersonNotEnrolledInBenefit at test case Enrollments null:
    the benefit of the parameters is "bogus".
    the person id of the parameters is "p1".
    q_d_check_result expects answers [].

scenario NOT_Enrolled_in_Bogus_Benefit is, as stated in the Bruno requests of PersonNotEnrolledInBenefit at test case NOT Enrolled in Bogus Benefit:
    the benefit of the parameters is "bogus".
    the person id of the parameters is "p1".
    the enrollments of the situation are listed.
    the enrollments of the situation include "p2" with "bogus".
    q_d_check_result expects answers ["the check result is true"].

query q_d_check_result is:
    the check result is which truth value.

